// XFAIL: RT-212: (fuller form of R302D-34) cloning a Vec, a tuple or an array of references fails inside std: `a.clone()` of a `Vec<&i64, Gpa>`, `extend_from_slice`, `to_vec_in`, `(&k, 1i64).clone()`, `[&k, &k].clone()` (0.30.2)
// rustc prints the EXPECT line (twin: r302d_034c_clone_of_containers_of_references.rs.txt).
// vole: `<std>:5759:23: error[type error] expected '&i64', got 'i64'` (std's
// Vec::extend_clones, `self.push(s[i].clone())`), and the same at the tuple's and
// the array's Clone (<std>:1596:10, <std>:7418:45): each clones an element place of
// type T = &i64 per instance, which finds i64's Clone (R302D-34). A Vec<&str>
// clones (str has no Clone), and `a.iter().cloned()`, `Some(&k).clone()` and
// `a.resize(3, &k)` work. v0.28.0, v0.29.0, v0.30.1 the same.
// EXPECT: [3] [3] [3] (3, 1) [3, 3]
fn main(gpa: Gpa) {
    let k = 3i64;
    let mut a: Vec<&i64, Gpa> = Vec::new_in(gpa);
    a.push(&k);
    let b = a.clone();
    let mut c: Vec<&i64, Gpa> = Vec::new_in(gpa);
    c.extend_from_slice(&a);
    let d = a.as_slice().to_vec_in(gpa);
    let t = (&k, 1i64);
    let u = t.clone();
    let arr = [&k, &k];
    let brr = arr.clone();
    println("{:?} {:?} {:?} {:?} {:?}", b, c, d, u, brr);
}
